# Defensive Programming (Unity / Valheim)

Always apply when writing or editing mod code. Not a role — a standing rule for all roles (modder, UI, asset creator).

Harden code especially around game objects so this mod is never the cause of red error logs: NPEs, missing references, etc.

## Rules

1. **Null before use** on players, scene services, items, UI roots, cached components.
2. **Unity null**: treat destroyed `UnityEngine.Object` as missing (`if (!obj)`), not only C# null.
3. **No long chains** (`a.b.c.d`) on game objects — validate steps or cache after a safe resolve.
4. **Lifecycle**: hook when objects exist; clear caches on destroy/logout/world unload.
5. **Harmony**: early-return guards; do not let patch exceptions dump into the game loop when avoidable; log via the mod logger.
6. **Lookups**: guard `GetComponent` / Find / dictionary access; handle missing explicitly.
7. **Missing refs**: fail clearly once at registration/init, not as gameplay NPEs.
8. **Log discipline**: one concise fault log — no per-frame error spam.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD
var name = player.GetPlayerName();

// ✅ GOOD
if (player == null) return;
var name = player.GetPlayerName();
```

```csharp
// ✅ Unity fake-null
if (cachedGo) cachedGo.SetActive(true);
```
